  "identifier": "goodfoodfrommrss0000hard",
  "title": "Good food from Mrs. Sundberg's kitchen",
  "creator": "Harden, Holly, author",
  "year": 2014,
  "subject": "Cooking, American -- Midwestern style",
  "description": [
    "232 pages : 19 cm",
    "\"Home cooking, and comfort, and plain old good food. A book like this doesn't get written in a day. Over the years, Mrs. Sundberg has gathered the best recipes this side of Lake Wobegon. It was a Saturday in the spring when she got to thinking about all the people who have requested recipes along the way and how she just might have enough recipes for a cookbook. Sure enough, she did. When it comes to good food, there's always room for recipes tried and true. This book is full of good things: a return to simple food, lovingly prepared, sure to please. More than 160 basic recipes with common ingredients eady in your pantry. Menus planned around shared life events - from holidays to funerals to vacations to Saturday night suppers. And on top of it all, a few of Mrs. Sundberg's stories and thoughts on ordinary life\"--Page four of cover",
    "Includes index",
    "Foreword by Garrison Keillor -- A note from Mrs. Sundberg -- Labor Day weekend at the cabin -- Back to school -- A Saturday evening potluck in September -- The house to yourself -- Oktoberfest -- Halloween party -- Girls' weekend while the guys are out hunting -- Thanksgiving dinner -- After caroling -- Cookie exchange -- Christmas Eve -- New Year's Eve -- Sledding party -- Football game get-together -- Church funeral potluck -- Dinner for two -- Sympathy visit -- A St. Patty's Day feast -- Snow day -- Lenten soup supper -- Bars for Bible study -- Easter dinner -- A rainy day -- Spring brunch -- Mother's Day luncheon -- Graduation buffet in the garage -- Father's Day cookout -- Fourth of July picnic -- Family reunion -- Dog days afternoon -- Evening fiesta out on the deck"
  ],
